    {
      "id": "015cea00-1041-4b85-a645-e71c64c86038",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Scope: updating CodeQL GitHub Actions to v4. Risk surface: CI behavior, analysis output, SARIF upload, gating logic.\n\nTesting protocol:\n\n1. **Local diff sanity**\n   - Change only the CodeQL action version.\n   - No workflow logic edits.\n   - Confirm matrix, languages, and triggers unchanged.\n\n2. **Dry-run CI on fork**\n   - Push branch to fork.\n   - Let all workflows run.\n   - Expect: green across non-CodeQL jobs first. Any unrelated failure is noise, not signal.\n\n3. **CodeQL-specific validation**\n   - Check the CodeQL job logs.\n   - Verify:\n     - Action pulls v4.x (explicitly shown in logs).\n     - Database creation succeeds.\n     - Analysis step completes without warnings about deprecated flags.\n     - SARIF upload step reports success.\n\n4. **Compare SARIF output**\n   - Download SARIF artifact from before and after.\n   - Ignore ordering differences.\n   - Watch for:\n     - Sudden zero findings (usually misconfig).\n     - Explosion of findings (query pack change or language mis-detection).\n   - Small deltas are expected across major versions.\n\n5. **Check query packs**\n   - Ensure the same query suites are used (e.g. `security-extended`, `security-and-quality`).\n   - v4 defaults may differ; explicit is safer.\n\n6. **Baseline enforcement**\n   - If repo uses “fail on new alerts”:\n     - Confirm baseline still applies.\n     - No unexpected CI failures due to reclassified alerts.\n\n7. **Cross-language edge cases**\n   - If multiple languages:\n     - Confirm each language step runs.\n     - No language silently skipped.\n\n8. **Re-run on main**\n   - Rebase branch on latest main.\n   - Re-run workflows to rule out transient CI issues.\n\n9. **Rollback check**\n   - Confirm reverting the version cleanly restores prior behavior.\n   - This proves the change is isolated.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- CI green.\n- CodeQL job completes.\n- SARIF uploads.\n- Alert delta explainable by CodeQL version change.\n- No workflow logic regressions.\n\nThat is sufficient to assert “not breaking anything.”",
      "timestamp": "2026-01-29T18:59:04.753Z",
