    {
      "id": "6ff2346a-b013-4733-ac7b-550a5d26c3f1",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Root cause is not CodeQL.\n\nWhat broke:\n- This step now executes on the branch/PR you pushed for the CodeQL change.\n- The workflow expects **repo secrets**:\n  - `BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME`\n  - `BROWSERSTACK_ACCESS_KEY`\n- They are **not available** in this execution context, so the action receives `username = empty` and hard-fails.\n\nWhy it shows up now:\n- Any CI change (including CodeQL) causes *all* jobs to re-run.\n- BrowserStack is unrelated but lives in the same workflow or required workflow set.\n- GitHub does **not** expose secrets to:\n  - Forked repos\n  - PRs from forks\n  - Some restricted contexts, depending on repo settings\n\nThe log confirms this:\n```\ngithub-token: none\nInput required and not supplied: username\n```\n\nThis is a **configuration / secrets availability issue**, not a regression from CodeQL v4.\n\nHow to classify this failure:\n- ❌ Not caused by CodeQL\n- ❌ Not a breaking change in your PR\n- ✅ Expected when secrets are missing\n\nMinimal, correct fixes (pick one that matches repo policy):\n\n1. **Gate the step on secret presence** (safest)\n```\nif: |\n  (github.event_name == 'push' || github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository)\n  && secrets.BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME != ''\n```\n\n2. **Disable BrowserStack on PRs**\n```\nif: github.event_name == 'push'\n```\n\n3. **Move BrowserStack to a separate workflow**\n- Keeps infra tests isolated\n- Prevents unrelated failures when touching CI tooling\n\nWhat you should state in the PR:\n- CodeQL upgrade verified\n- Failure is from BrowserStack secrets not being available in this run\n- No behavioral change introduced by the CodeQL update\n\nThis does **not** block merging a CodeQL version bump unless the project explicitly requires BrowserStack on every CI run.",
