    {
      "id": "7bfe7da1-d221-4ca2-8eba-85b291571505",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This failure is also **not caused by the CodeQL change**.\n\nClassification first, then mechanics.\n\n## What failed\n- **IE11-mode E2E test on Windows**\n- Selenium error:\n  ```\n  ElementClickInterceptedError\n  Other element would receive the click: <div class=\"modal-header\">\n  ```\n- Test logic reached application state successfully.\n- Failure occurs during a UI interaction, not setup.\n\n## Why this is happening\nThis is a **classic flaky Selenium + IE11-mode issue**.\n\nFacts from the log:\n- App loaded correctly.\n- Archive loaded correctly.\n- Prior navigation steps passed.\n- Failure occurs on a click where a modal/header overlaps the target.\n- IE11 mode has:\n  - Broken hit-testing\n  - Poor z-index handling\n  - Timing/layout instability\n- Selenium’s click is **coordinate-based**, not semantic.\n- Minor timing or layout differences cause interception.\n\nNothing in a CodeQL version bump:\n- Touches runtime JS\n- Changes DOM\n- Affects E2E behavior\n- Alters Node, Selenium, or browser versions\n\nThis test would fail intermittently even on a no-op commit.\n\n## Signal that this is infra flakiness\n- 9 passing, 1 pending, 1 failing\n- Failure after ~40s of successful execution\n- Error is **ElementClickIntercepted**, not assertion failure\n- IE11-only test\n- Same test likely passes on rerun\n\n## Correct handling in context of your PR\nThis is **non-blocking noise** relative to a CI tooling change.\n\nWhat maintainers typically accept:\n- CI failures unrelated to touched code\n- Especially for:\n  - Legacy browsers\n  - IE11 compatibility suites\n  - Known flaky Selenium tests\n\nWhat you should state clearly in the PR discussion:\n- CodeQL update verified\n- Failure is in IE11-mode E2E test\n- Error is Selenium click interception\n- Test reaches expected state before failure\n- No code affecting UI or E2E touched\n- This test is known to be flaky / legacy-browser-sensitive\n\n## What you should *not* do\n- Do not attempt to “fix” the test in a CodeQL PR\n- Do not change timing, waits, or selectors\n- Do not mask the failure unless maintainers request it\n\n## If asked to justify merging\nYour justification is simple and defensible:\n- Change is isolated to GitHub Actions CodeQL version\n- Two failures observed:\n  1. BrowserStack secrets missing\n  2. IE11 Selenium flake\n- Neither is causally connected to the change\n- Core CI and CodeQL job itself are sound\n\nThis is sufficient to proceed.",
